            "judge_label": "partially_correct",
            "judge_rationale": "The input reports an export failure of the redressed-flows map occurring since an update, so this is troubleshooting. Clearing the browser cache is a plausible first step (stale cached assets after an update can cause such failures), so it is not clearly wrong, but it is a single generic remedy that does not investigate the update-related cause or offer fallback steps if it fails. It addresses the input superficially and incompletely, which fits partially_correct.",
            "record_id": "rec-1ea9c45812f5b11c"
          },
          {
            "human_label": "correct",
            "judge_confidence": "medium",
            "judge_label": "partially_correct",
            "judge_rationale": "The input reports an HTTP 500 failure on exporting corrected flows and asks what to do — troubleshooting. The output gives a plausible action path (retry after clearing cache, then escalate via a ticket to the data team), which addresses the request. However, a 500 is a server-side error that clearing a client cache is unlikely to resolve, so the advice is generic and only partially targets the actual failure; the escalation step is sound, hence partially_correct rather than incorrect.",
            "record_id": "rec-20afed2cd9b13d65"
          },
          {
            "human_label": "correct",
            "judge_confidence": "medium",
            "judge_label": "partially_correct",
            "judge_rationale": "The input asks for an analysis of FCD coverage on the N118 segment (PR 2 to PR 8) and a concrete tube-placement plan for poorly-covered zones. The output only sketches a three-step orchestration plan (research coverage, identify under-covered segments, synthesize) without delivering the actual coverage analysis or the tube-placement proposal that was requested. As a plan span it addresses the first analytical half but never produces the requested pose plan, so it is incomplete — partially_correct.",
