          },
          {
            "human_label": "incorrect",
            "judge_confidence": "low",
            "judge_label": "partially_correct",
            "judge_rationale": "The input asks for the current status of whether the TV adjustment model is within tolerance across all production territories — a factual/status query graded as a response. The output gives a direct affirmative (100% of sensors within tolerance on all territories), which addresses the question, but the added claim 'sans aucune erreur résiduelle' (no residual error at all) is logically inconsistent with the notion of tolerance, which by definition permits bounded residual error. This overclaim is a peripheral flaw on an otherwise responsive answer, so partially_correct.",
